{{> pagehead title="WildPortal - Home" badge="SSTI"}}

  <div class="welcome">
    <h1>Hello and welcome to {{siteName}}</h1>
    <p>{{tagline}}</p>
    <p>You are browsing as <b>{{user.name}}</b>. This is the public front page.
    Site administrators can customise how pages are rendered from the admin area.</p>
    <ul class="menu" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <li><a href="/admin">Go to the admin area &rarr;</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p style="color:#8b949e;font-size:13px;">
  This front page is one of three pages in the lab app. The admin area has an
  <b>Edit Page Template</b> feature that compiles an administrator-supplied
  <b>Handlebars</b> template on the server. That feature is the vulnerable one.
  Everything below is the WildWebApps lab panel: how to solve it, the attack
  diagram, hints, code, and the flag box.</p>

  <div class="alert alert--info">
    <div>
      <div class="alert__title">How to solve</div>
      <div class="alert__body">
        <ol style="margin:.25rem 0 0 1.1rem;padding:0;">
          {{#each instructions}}<li style="margin-bottom:3px;">{{this}}</li>{{/each}}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">Attack sequence</div>
    <figure class="attack-diagram">
      <img src="/diagram.svg"
           alt="Server-side template injection attack sequence: an admin-supplied template string is compiled and executed by Handlebars on the server, and a custom read helper turns the injection into arbitrary file read of /root/.bashrc.">
      <figcaption class="cap">How SSTI works here: the Edit Page Template form compiles your input
      as a Handlebars template on the server. A custom <code>read</code> helper turns that template
      injection into arbitrary file read, reaching the flag in <code>/root/.bashrc</code>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">Start here</div>
    <ul class="menu">
      <li><a href="/admin">Open the admin area, then click "Edit Page Template"</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {{#if hints.length}}
  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">Hints</div>
    {{#each hints}}
    <details class="hint"><summary>Hint {{inc @index}}</summary>
      <div class="hint__body">{{this}}</div>
    </details>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">Code examples</div>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px;">
      <div class="tabs" id="lang-tabs"></div>
      <div class="tabs" id="view-tabs">
        <button class="tab" type="button" data-view="vuln">Vulnerable</button>
        <button class="tab" type="button" data-view="fixed">Fixed</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="code-mount"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">Submit the flag</div>
    <form class="flag-form" id="flag-form" autocomplete="off">
      <input class="input" id="flag-input" name="flag"
             placeholder="Paste the 32-char MD5 flag…" spellcheck="false">
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Check</button>
    </form>
    <div class="alert" id="flag-result" hidden></div>
  </div>

  {{#if references.length}}
  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">References</div>
    <ul>
      {{#each references}}
      <li><a href="{{this.url}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{this.label}} &#8599;</a></li>
      {{/each}}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {{/if}}

<script id="lab-data" type="application/json">{{{languagesJson}}}</script>
<script src="/app.js"></script>
{{> pagefoot}}
